# Git already stores every text file with LF. Without this file each contributor's
# core.autocrlf decides what lands in their working tree, and on Windows that means
# CRLF -- which Prettier (endOfLine: "lf") then reports as a style violation on files
# nobody has touched. Pin LF everywhere so `npx prettier --check .` agrees on all
# platforms and `--write .` doesn't rewrite the whole tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts that genuinely want CRLF
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets -- never convert
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.tga binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary
